From c2d24a32dcbecea8328abe890d0ff5ae89cecd34 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dinadur <59811564+dinadur@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 22:31:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/18] B70: product delivery fixes from the 20-prompt run

Of 20 Telegram product requests on 2026-10-07, 11 were withheld. Causes fixed:

- Target parsing: a full stop after a digit was never a sentence end, so
  'comparing ... Honeywell Home T9. Use each manufacturer's ...' made the last
  target swallow the next sentence (bogus targets such as 'warranty'); the
  'research X for' clause could also run across sentences. Sentence ends are
  now any [.!?] not followed by a digit, and target clauses stay inside one
  sentence ('Aventon Level.2' still parses). All 10 named-comparison prompts
  now yield their three products; viability replay makes 3 previously
  withheld turns receipt-ready.
- Turn window: a length/network continuation nudge ended the current-turn
  window, resetting search/extract counts to 0 and causing
  RESEARCH_RECEIPT_ERROR; such nudges are now skipped like synthetic rows.
- A receipt/terminal call after searches but no extraction is rewritten into
  the first extraction (round-robin over search batches, one URL per family).
- Alternative coverage ignores parenthetical qualifiers; the quality-first
  repair nudge names the missing alternatives and, for missing citations,
  lists the citable receipt URLs; rejected drafts log defects and missing
  alternatives.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
